> wouldn't it make more sense to define some lang item wrapper that unsafely forces co/contravariance on a type param?

That would be awesome. Perhaps it would emit a compile-time error if the inline layout of the type depends on that parameter at all… AH, but what if
```rust
struct Foo<#[unsafe(force_covariant)] T: AssocIsARef>(T::Assoc);

/// # Safety
/// `Assoc` must be `&'a U` for some lifetime `'a` and some type `U: Sized`.
unsafe trait AssocIsARef {
    type Assoc;
}
