soooo perhaps `struct Foo<#[unsafe(force_covariant)] T>(T::Assoc);` has undefined behavior but no hard compile-time error (could be a lint though), or maybe it’s “merely” unsound (due to the potential to e.g. wrap it into `Box<Foo<T>>`).

In any case… the safety requirements on `force_co(ntra)variant` would certainly be interesting.

